\f1\fs22 The artificial mediocrity that governed the judgment of the compound\'92s security system recognised the huddled masses trapped inside its gates, made a threat assessment and decided what the situation required was food and shelter. Within a quarter of an hour, Shakti security and catering staff had carted enough provisions to the lawns north of the carpark for an encampment to spring up like mushrooms in warm rain on roo shit. Campfires of gum branches gathered from the roadside to the gates crackled and flickered. Folks danced and played guitars loaned to them by the Elvi while a remnant stayed at the gate and impotently chanted slogans about what they wanted and how long they weren\'92t prepared to wait for it.\
