\f1\fs22 Around eight, while the Southern Cross tried to peer in through the compound\'92s light haze, a hover-copt safely landed on the pad, artificial mediocrity judging that, under no circumstances, would Eloise want to shoot down a flagship whirly-gig registered to Hardy Industries. Uncharacteristically making two correct decisions within minutes, it had fed and sheltered potential rioters, and avoided blowing particles of Chanta and his entourage of Elvi and Jones clones to elevations where Acrux, Mimosa, Gacrux, Imai, and Ginan could easily have observed them without telescopes.\
Once all the fans had been powered down, the forward port door opened and a contingent of Jones clones secured the pad, then came the Elvi securing their coiffed hair and capes. Only when a Jones clone radioed back that they detected no new conspiracy theories was Chanta allowed on the tarmac.\
By that time, enough Elvi to run and perform in a travelling circus had surrounded the hover pad, among them the High Elvis.\
\'93Great Teacher and Wise Humper,\'94 the High Elvis began formally, \'93We are honoured to have you at our vigil.\'94\
\'93Thanks,\'94 Chanta said. \'93I needed a night out.\'94 He looked about at the scene illuminated by the pulses of the stage lighting at the far end of the carpark. A party was obviously in progress. \'93Is it safe for the girls to come out?\'94 Chanta asked and found himself coughing by the end of it. \'93Tax, this air is clean. I think it\'92s stripping gunk out of my lungs that got there in primary school.\'94\
\'93There is an uneasy peace between Eloise and Alexander security factions, but no one seems to be firing on anyone out of uniform.\'94\
\'93What about the Dick Tracys?\'94 Chanta asked as he glanced at the ring of Jones clone backs.\
\'93Uncertain,\'94 the High Elvis said.\
Chanta looked about then waved the Elvisettes down from the hover-copt. \'93Where is the Holy Momma?\'94\
\'93We understand Eloise has her secured.\'94\
Chanta grimaced and rolled his shoulders. \'93That woman seems to keep stealing her away from us.\'94\
\'93I agree, Wise\'97\'94\
Chanta waved down the rest of the titling, and pulled out his device. Before he could dial, it rang.\
\'93Tony.\'94\
\'93Sarah, I was just about to call you.\'94\
\'93What are you doing here?\'94\
The clean air stuck in Chanta\'92s throat again. \'93News travels fast.\'94\
\'93Hayley saw you land.\'94 Sarah swallowed. \'93There are cameras everywhere.\'94\
Chanta looked for one and waved at the most likely places to mount several.\
\'93You\'92re such a boofhead,\'94 Sarah said.\
\'93You can see me waving?\'94\
\'93No, but I can guess you are doing something silly. And kinda cute.\'94\
Chanta blinked his eyes; they were getting rather too misty. \'93I\'92ve been doing cleaning jobs.\'94\
\'93Murder scenes?\'94 Sarah asked.\
\'93I wish,\'94 Chanta joked. \'93Nah, just some other apartments in the building. Kinda boring, really. The hardest thing is getting the cocaine out of the carpet and the sofas. Takes some forensic attention, I can tell you.\'94\
Sarah smiled and somehow Chanta felt it. \'93Is Little Clinton arriving soon?\'94 he asked.\
\'93Kathy thinks so. I keep thinking it\'92s all starting, but the contractions are still sporadic. At this rate, Kathy says it might all start with a gush.\'94\
\'93Spectacular.\'94\
They spent some seconds in awkward silence. \'93The Elvi want to be with you,\'94 Chanta said.\
\'93I know.\'94\
\'93I\'85\'94 Chanta started, and trailed off.\
\'93I know. But don\'92t get yourself into trouble up there.\'94\
\'93Where are you?\'94\
\'93In a bunker with Eloise.\'94\
\'93And Kathy and Hayley.\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93Anyone else?\'94\
\'93No.\'94\
Chanta let it slide for an extended few seconds, then, \'93I saw Alexander\'92s show\'85\'94\
\'93Oh.\'94\
\'93Yeah. We\'92re old friends, you know.\'94\
\'93Yes, I did know that.\'94\
\'93I saw how you saved Eloise\'85 is she okay?\'94\
\'93Yes. Never better. You know Eloise.\'94\
